- Story & Context: Years after the original projection collective was evicted from Glasgow’s East End, urban spelunkers cracked the padlocks of The Grosvenor to discover the screen had decayed into a massive, shimmering web of blackened silver nitrate and dead chrysalises. When air currents from the subway tunnels rushed through the ventilation shafts, the iron rafters began humming in perfect unison with the band's abandoned drone resonators, producing an unholy acoustic skirl that shook plaster down on the trespassers. Legend says the phantom audio head still plays the score to an unmade silent catastrophe film, its looped final scream echoing against the rubble: "Leave your dead shells beneath the seats!"
